  "what_the_train_exemplars_store_is": "SLURP v2 base program module M1 / cell B1, read unmodified on the fresh DEV-2000-ADDED roster: the top-20 TRAIN construction-pool exemplars (excluding every utterance with a recording in TRAIN Fold A, Fold B or DEV-1000; 9,354-facet pool) recalled by cosine against this row's OWN sealed DEV-2000-ADDED speech vector, ranked by saea-rank-wcos-prior-agree-v1 (identity on cosine: w_cos=1, w_prior=0, w_agree=0) and passed through saea-fuse-supplyfilter-v1 with m=c=top_l=20 -- twenty in, twenty out on every row, the same 'no coverage reshaping' discipline cell KU-S3 established. Each value renders as '<utterance> | <scenario>_<action> | type=filler; ...' (KB view annotated-exemplars, scripts/build_knowledge_snapshot.py). The decision is delivered to the SOLVER phase (the program's LAST phase) through the E6 acquire transition, exactly as on TRAIN Fold A; the Solver's instruction bytes are byte-identical to the unmodified cell PLAN's. The composed acquire transition also carries the slot-contracts store's own candidate_supply.solver decision on the same wave; both compose into one PhaseSupply via rails.knowledge_stores._compose_supplies.",
  "what_this_is": "Cell B6 plan arm (owner decisions 34, 35, 78, 79, 86, 88): the locked v2.0 default plan (cell PLAN's fragment: the sealed B1-notool base plus slot-contracts v2, deliver_normaliser v3 and the review-loop marker 'on') flown unmodified on the fresh DEV-2000-ADDED roster (1,000 rows, split identity ee6c43cd4dd8fc2a583d2dd053e799c2d002efa3755fcd092ba7c7565431bf67) instead of TRAIN Fold A. Only the roster-bound bindings move: the dataset fragment, the promoted speech packets, the two row-side query_source pins (both stores' query vectors are this roster's own, built model-free by scripts/build_slurp_query_content_derivative.py for the content dimension and by the prior DEV-2000-ADDED speech-query encoding pass for the intent-boundary dimension), the preparation_source_receipts, the devel-gold scorer and the per-flight ids. The native_episode block, phase_material, policy, all three knowledge-store releases/snapshots, the geometry and the E13/E20/E22 declarations stay byte-identical to cell PLAN. This is a fresh-roster generalisation read of an already-locked plan, not a new form: no smoke is registered because the form has already been flown on TRAIN Fold A (cell PLAN) and left no open form question. Any second failure closes this generation flight. Neither this baseline nor cell B6's readiness requirements carry a prepared_phase_supply pin: this cell's own first-phase Perception supply is built model-free by scripts/flights/repin_cell.py at flip time, so this registration writes nothing under $SPEECHRL_DATA_DIR beyond the query-content derivative of item 1.",
